## Context
Audit of inline SKILL.md code (2026-10-11): `skills/molt/SKILL.md` holds about 30
lines of untested ticket-close logic (close, archive, stage, prune duplicates in
`tickets/` vs `tickets/closed/`), the same job roar does inline (ticket 1084
scripts roar's copy). Two defects ride along:
- The merged-branch probe (bash block near line 239) uses GNU-only `grep -oP`,
  parses `ls`, and derives the ticket from the branch with `t\K\d+`; a branch
  not named `tN…` yields nothing and the probe reports "not merged" silently.
- The Zotero reconcile block writes the fixed path `/tmp/zotero-reconcile.json`;
  parallel sessions clobber each other.

## Exit criteria
- [x] The close / archive / stage / duplicate-prune blocks become one script (shared with 1084's roar script if it has landed, otherwise placed so 1084 can reuse it), with tests for close-already-moved, archive-reported paths, and the duplicate prune
- [x] The merged-branch probe uses `git merge-base --is-ancestor` (or the PR squash-subject check as a second signal), portable grep only, and reports "could not determine" rather than "not merged" when it cannot map a branch
- [x] The reconcile output path is per-session (`mktemp`), not a fixed `/tmp` name
- [x] `skills/molt/SKILL.md` calls the script instead of inline blocks
